## 1️⃣ Largest Element in a List

**Problem:**  
Find the largest element in an array of integers.

**Description:**  
Given an array of positive integers, identify and return the largest element. This is one of the basic array traversal problems that lays the groundwork for understanding array operations.

**Resource:**  
[GeeksforGeeks - Find Largest Element in Array](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/find-largest-element-array/)

---

## 2️⃣ Check if Array is Sorted

**Problem:**  
Determine whether a given array is sorted in non-decreasing order.

**Description:**  
Given an array, check if the elements are sorted from smallest to largest. This helps in understanding array traversal with conditional checks and early termination.

**Resource:**  
[GeeksforGeeks - Check if Array is Sorted](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/program-check-array-sorted-not/)

---

## 3️⃣ Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array

**Problem:**  
Remove duplicate elements from a sorted array in-place and return the new length.

**Description:**  
Given a sorted array, remove the duplicates so that each element appears only once. Modify the array in place and return the length of the updated array. This problem is essential to understand two-pointer techniques and in-place modification.

**Resource:**  
[LeetCode - Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array](https://leetcode.com/problems/remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array/)

